[h3]Content Adjustments[/h3]
[olist]
[*] Optimized the enemy HP growth mechanism;
[*] The "Shield of Fortitude" has been adjusted from being destroyed after 3 battles to being destroyed after 12 times;
[*] Boss skill "Making 1 random piece(s) unable to make action per turn" has been adjusted to last for only one turn.
[/olist]

[olist]
[*] The action order of one-time pieces and "Fusion Capsule" has been adjusted;
[*] When the "Mucus Hunter" eliminates a "Slime", it will obtain the enchantment of the Slime itself at the same time;
[*] The problem of excessive actions when the "Cross-dresser" and the "Coder" are present simultaneously has been optimized;
[*] The issue of lag in the late stage of the game has been further optimized.
[/olist]

Hi, hunters!

We’re thrilled to announce that Lucky Hunter, the Roguelike game combining deck-building and auto-chess elements, officially launches today! The game is priced 5.99USD, with a 20% launch discount for the first two weeks. If you’re interested, feel free to check it out!

https://store.steampowered.com/app/2824310/

Compared to the demo, the official version brings a lot of new content, including

[*]A wide variety of new pieces and artifacts. The official version includes hundreds of pieces and artifacts, along with a large number of "Advanced Artifacts" that allow you to fuse two different pieces into an advanced piece, adding even more possibilities to the game; 
[*] 9 brand-new builds for you to explore;
[*] Build your collection and strive for completion with the brand new "collection" feature!; 
[*]A "Normal Mode" with 4 levels. After completing this mode, you’ll unlock an endless mode featuring more maps, enemies, and the “Altar” that allows you to break level limits.; 

Additionally, you can give gifts to NPCs to obtain powerful, permanently hidden artifacts, and there are multiple save slots to allow for different playthrough styles. Dive into the game to discover all the content waiting for you!

